Subject: The baseline tier must not treat a `gosub` as a droppable sentinel

What this does
  The baseline tier must not treat a `gosub` as a droppable sentinel.

Why we need it
  The baseline tier's identity model performs a real parallel copy for a stack shaper, so a `gosub`'s return address is a register move where the optimising path aliases it. The sentinel marking then made an unrelated later hand-`OP_drop` remove a `finally` continuation the baseline's address-based control stack still owned, so `break` out of nested `try/finally` raised `InternalError: register VM: no continuation to return to` (`tos-cache-exceptions.js`, `nested finally with break`).

What it adds
  The `OP_gosub` sentinel bit is not set for the baseline tier (`!fd->regvm_baseline`); the continuation is owned and popped by `ROP_finally_leave` alone.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 437910a..02760b5 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -65875,8 +65875,15 @@ static __exception int js_regvm_encode(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionDef *fd,
                         sentinel_bits[push_base[pos] + 2] = 1;
                 } else if (op2 == OP_catch) {
                     sentinel_bits[push_base[pos]] = 1;
-                } else if (op2 == OP_gosub) {
-                    /* the return address is a slot with no value in it */
+                } else if (op2 == OP_gosub && !fd->regvm_baseline) {
+                    /* The return address is a slot with no value, so a hand
+                       `OP_drop` of it removes the control-stack entry (the
+                       sentinel convention of `regvm_lower`). The baseline tier
+                       must not mark it: its control stack is address-based
+                       (`ROP_finally_enter`/`ROP_finally_leave`), and its shape
+                       expansion moves the operand stack around the gosub push,
+                       so a set `sentinel_bit` would let an unrelated hand-drop
+                       remove a continuation whose finally has not run. */
                     sentinel_bits[push_base[pos]] = 1;
                 }
             }
